  "about_link": "About",
  "about_back": "Results",
  "about_title": "About MatdaanPulse",
  "about_intro": "MatdaanPulse tracks Indian election results for the Lok Sabha and Vidhan Sabhas: live counting, interactive maps, alliance tallies and seat-by-seat detail. It is an independent project built by MatdaanPulse.",
  "about_disclaimer_title": "Not an official source",
  "about_disclaimer_body": "MatdaanPulse is not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to the Election Commission of India (ECI) or any political party. Numbers here can contain errors or lag behind official figures. For official results, always check the ECI.",
  "about_disclaimer_link": "Official ECI results",
  "about_data_title": "Where the data comes from",
  "about_data_intro": "We want to be open about the quality of every dataset. Some older elections are incomplete or partly estimated, and we are correcting them. Here is exactly what each one contains today.",
  "about_quality_legend": "Data quality key",
  "about_quality_real": "Real votes",
  "about_quality_partial": "Partly incomplete",
  "about_quality_estimated": "Votes estimated",
  "about_quality_real_desc": "vote counts as published",
  "about_quality_partial_desc": "real votes, some fields missing or wrong",
  "about_quality_estimated_desc": "winners and margins are real, vote counts are not",
  "about_source": "Source",
  "about_source_unknown": "not recorded",
  "about_note_all_candidates": "Every candidate, with real vote counts.",
  "about_note_top5_nota": "Top 5 candidates and NOTA per seat; other candidates are not included.",
  "about_note_two_candidates": "Only the winner and runner-up per seat.",
  "about_note_winner_only": "Only the winner per seat; runner-ups are missing.",
  "about_note_votes_from_margin": "Vote counts are estimated: only the winning margin is real (runner-up set to 50,000 votes, winner to 50,000 + margin). Vote share, swing and vote-split charts are not meaningful for this election.",
  "about_note_placeholder_names": "Candidate names are missing (shown as \"<party> Candidate\"), and the runner-up is a placeholder with unknown party.",
  "about_note_turnout_unreliable": "Turnout and elector counts are unreliable and do not match the vote totals.",
  "about_note_reserved_wrong": "SC/ST reserved seats are not marked; every seat shows as General.",
  "about_note_seats_postponed": "232 of 234 seats: polls in Aravakurichi and Thanjavur were postponed and are not included.",
  "about_note_seat_countermanded": "146 of 147 seats: the Patkura poll was countermanded and held later; it is not in ECI's report and not included.",
  "about_note_sangha_seat": "Sangha (seat 32) is elected by the registered monks and nuns of Sikkim's monasteries and has no territory, so the map shows 31 seats.",
  "about_note_unopposed_seats": "Some seats were won unopposed (no poll): they count for their winner but have no votes, margin or turnout.",
  "about_note_ocr_scan": "ECI's report is a scanned report, read by OCR; every figure was checked against the report's own totals, and the few misreads were corrected from the scan.",
  "about_note_undivided_2009": "The 2009 assembly was elected for undivided Andhra Pradesh (294 seats); shown are the 175 seats of today's Andhra Pradesh, renumbered, with no majority line.",
  "about_note_jk_boundaries_1995": "The state's assembly on the 1995 boundaries (87 seats, Ladakh's 4 included); 2008 and 2014 are compared with each other only.",
  "about_note_jk_boundaries_2022": "The union territory's 90 seats under the 2022 delimitation; no earlier election shares these boundaries, so seats have no history. The 5 nominated members are not shown.",
  "about_note_source_unrecorded": "The original source was not recorded.",
  "about_data_other": "Districts and regions (such as Mithila or Seemanchal) are our own groupings, not official units. Links between one person's contests across Bihar elections are matched by name and may contain mistakes.",
  "about_live_title": "How live counting works",
  "about_live_body": "On counting day, results on MatdaanPulse refresh automatically about every 10–15 seconds, so you don't need to reload. Our figures can trail the official count by a short time.",
  "about_live_leading": "Leading: the candidate is ahead in the votes counted so far. The lead can still change.",
  "about_live_won": "Won: counting is complete and the result has been declared.",
